"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, powerwashsimulator.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder within the Archipelago Launcher directory. BepInEx will then be downloaded into the PowerWash Simulator game directory, along with the required mods, which will be placed in PowerWashSimulator\\BepInEx\\plugins. The game will then launch and automatically close after a few seconds to ensure BepInEx is properly initialized.\nThe first launch after setup may take longer than usual (around 40 seconds).",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"PowerWash Simulator is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file (powerwashsimulator.apworld). When the apworld is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once everything is set up, a new 'AP Client' window should appear on the left side of your screen in PowerWash Simulator.\n\nIn the 'Address:port' field, enter archipelago.gg: followed by the port. This is a 5-digit number that you can find on the website after creating a new room.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it blank.\n\nIn 'Slot', enter the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nFinally, click 'Connect' and then, you can start a new run!",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"You have 2 revert options, both can't be enabled at the same time.\n\nIf you use the 'Clear AP Mods' option it will only delete the mods that are required for PowerWash Archipelago.\n\nIf you use the 'Full Clear BepInEx' option it will delete everything related to BepInEx and mods. If other mods are detected an additionnal confirmation will appear.",
